          "distinct": false,
          "id": "6aa6203de5891f98f38e2401c7f584106e737274",
          "message": "feat(solid): faithful odrl:isAnyOf/isNoneOf mapping in the ODRL->ACP bridge (sq-5fkpp) [FABLE-5] (#1920)\n\nmap_constraints_to_agents previously routed both set operators through the\ncatch-all to AgentMapping::Unmappable, freezing the whole rule one-shot.\nNow, matching how sparq-policy evaluates them (sq-uaz85):\n\n- recipient isAnyOf <set> -> one re-checked auth:agent head per member\n  (shares the isPartOf arm; the evaluator matches both operators as the\n  same flat lexical set). Empty/numeric operand stays Unmappable.\n- recipient isNoneOf <set> -> one ACP noneOf auth:exceptMatcher per member\n  (the list-valued neq dual, sq-5037). Fail-closed guards kept: a\n  numeric/dateTime operand (never satisfied by the evaluator's\n  set_negation_representable) and the degenerate EMPTY set stay one-shot;\n  a reserved-encoded member anywhere in the set sinks the whole rule to\n  one-shot via the existing condition_excepts length guard (dropping just\n  that member would re-admit it).\n\nTests: bridge<->evaluator parity panels on both operators (non-vacuous:\n5/9 new tests fail on the pre-change routing), per-member shape asserts,\nmalformed-operand/empty-set/reserved-member fail-closed guards, and the\nprohibition conditional-deny dual with deny-overrides. SKILL mapping\ntables updated (usage-control-policy, access-control).\n\nFeature-gated surface: sparq-solid `odrl-bridge` (OFF by default;\ncount-enforcement state also green).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-11T09:40:33Z",
